Build the game inside the engine's framework rather than beside it. The engine
owns the frame loop and the delta time it hands each tick, rendering and the
camera the mine is scrolled with, the input actions, the audio, asset loading,
and the on-screen debug overlay, and the game is written as subclasses of its
classes: a game instance, a game mode, actors and their components, and the
controllers that drive them. The engine constructs, ticks, and renders them in a
fixed order. Register what the game needs with the engine and use what it gives
back.
